  "publicacion": {
    "titulo": "The president's party lost Congress. The Dow jumped 1,569 points.",
    "descripcion": "The Dow rose 1,569 points (3%) on Nov. 4, 2026, its biggest post-midterm day since 1982, per CFRA data via CNN. The market had reasons beyond who won: some investors feared a drawn-out fight over the results, and futures fell Tuesday night before Trump told The New York Times he was \"absolutely willing\" to accept them. Brent crude fell 8.7% to $94.62 on hopes the Iran war could end. Not everything rose: an AI infrastructure fund lost 9% as data centers became a campaign issue. The S&P 500 has been up in the 12 months after all 19 midterms since 1950, which is a small sample and no guarantee. Chart: Dow close-to-close move the day after each midterm, 1994-2026, our calculation from Yahoo Finance closes. Non-partisan market explainer.",
